+% --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+% v1.3.21: the dictionary to the standard variables. Audit item I2-5.
+\subsection{The dictionary to the standard variables}
+\label{sec:theta-dictionary}
+
+Every gate in this bundle scores $\tau_\ell$ against $\tau_\ell$ and every
+external comparator is written in $\Theta_\ell$, so the map between them is
+load bearing in exactly one place and invisible everywhere else. The pieces
+are in three separated statements above and in Appendix~F; this is the one
+place they are composed.
+
+The direction dependence of a scalar mode is the contraction of the PSTF basis
+with $\hat k$. Its leading term is $\mu^\ell$ and trace removal supplies the
+rest, which is the Legendre polynomial up to normalisation:
+\begin{equation}
+  e^{\langle a_1\cdots a_\ell\rangle}\hat k_{a_1}\cdots\hat k_{a_\ell}
+  =\beta_\ell\,P_\ell(\mu),\qquad
+  \beta_\ell=\frac{\ell!}{(2\ell-1)!!},\qquad \mu=e\cdot\hat k .
+  \label{eq:pstf-legendre}
+\end{equation}
+Against the standard expansion
+$\Theta=\sum_\ell(-\mathrm i)^\ell(2\ell+1)\Theta_\ell P_\ell(\mu)$, term by
+term in $P_\ell$,
+\begin{equation}
+  \Theta_\ell=\frac{\mathrm i^\ell}{\alpha_\ell}\,\tau_\ell,
+  \qquad
+  \alpha_\ell=\frac{2\ell+1}{\beta_\ell}
+             =\frac{(2\ell+1)(2\ell-1)!!}{\ell!} .
+  \label{eq:theta-dictionary}
+\end{equation}
+
+\begin{center}\small
+\begin{tabular}{@{}lrrrrrr@{}}
+\toprule
+$\ell$ & 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 \\
+\midrule
+$\beta_\ell$  & $1$ & $1$ & $2/3$ & $2/5$ & $8/35$ & $8/63$ \\
+$\alpha_\ell$ & $1$ & $3$ & $15/2$ & $35/2$ & $315/8$ & $693/8$ \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabular}
+\end{center}
+
+\noindent
+$\alpha_2=15/2$ is the value \S\ref{sec:ell-zero-row} records the bundle as
+carrying and the value its kernel argument needs; Appendix~F's
+$\alpha_\ell^{-1}\tau_\ell$ is \eqref{eq:theta-dictionary} with the phase
+stripped; and the $\mathrm i^\ell$ is the one the \emph{Annals~I} convention
+already fixes. The dictionary is therefore read off this document rather than
+imported into it.
+
+\paragraph{The two ends, and the dipole checks itself.} $\alpha_0=1$, so
+$\Theta_0=\delta\tilde T$ exactly --- the $\tau_0\equiv0$ convention keeps the
+monopole out of the conversion altogether. $\alpha_1=3$, so
+$\Theta_1=\mathrm i\tau_1/3$, which makes $\tau_1$ the photon velocity in the
+convention where $\Theta_1=v_\gamma/3$. \eqref{eq:152-peak} is then the photon
+Euler equation for $v_\gamma$ rather than for $\Theta_1$, and
+\eqref{eq:153-peak}'s $+\tfrac k3\tilde\tau_1$ is $\Theta_0'=-k\Theta_1$ with
+the same factor of three. Neither was arranged to come out that way.
+
+\paragraph{The spectrum cannot adjudicate this, because $\alpha_\ell$ cancels
+from every ratio it forms.} $\alpha_\ell$ is
+\emph{defined} as $(2\ell+1)/\beta_\ell$, so it cancels from every internal
+ratio --- which is \S\ref{sec:spectrum}'s point. A wrong $\alpha_\ell$ would
+therefore pass every gate in this bundle and corrupt only criterion~5b, where
+the comparison is against codes written in $\Theta_\ell$. That is the whole
+reason this subsection exists.
+
 
